+## Isolated upstream 0.7 candidate handoff (2026-10-29)
+
+`platform/ps5/prepare-upstream-source.ps1 -AcceptVersionResolution` exports
+upstream `da1f775e686ebe47fa5848c723f7efba73d59211` and three-way reconciles
+tracked local changes using common base `49341628f0756817ab997b3ae8d75e98201cc47b`.
+It creates a new ignored candidate, merge snapshots and a revision/conflict
+manifest. It does not change the checkout, index or submodule pins. The explicit
+switch accepts only the recognized CMake project-version/PS5-opt-in conflict;
+other conflicts require resolution in that generated candidate. Upstream 0.7
+gameplay and crash-report source changes remain present. The upstream crash
+reporter itself has no PS5 implementation; retaining it does not add one.
+
+`build-game.ps1 -SourceRoot <candidate>/src` builds that isolated source using
+the preserved PsyZ pin. `-Resume <candidate-build>` rejects changing source roots.
+`-SDL3Prefix`, `-SDL3Source` and `-SDL3Build` select a matching installed library,
+generated source and build configuration explicitly, including on resume.
+The real candidate ELF linked at
+`outputs/ps5/game-20261029T053325Z-c0bd4a/b/parasite-eve-ps5.elf`:
